@baseUrl = http://localhost:9001

# New-device login alerts. Every login sets the long-lived `ogen_device`
# cookie. The account's first device is enrolled silently; a later login
# without that cookie (another browser, or a cleared cookie jar) queues the
# `new_device_login` email, whose "This wasn't me" link carries the token below.
#
# To get a token locally: log in once (sessions/sessions.http), clear the
# ogen_device cookie, log in again, then take `token=` from the secure_url in
# the queued send_email job's args (river_job.args->'vars'->>'secure_url').
@alertToken = paste-token-here

### Preview the alert — read-only, safe for mail scanners (expects 200; status pending|used|expired)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/security/login-alerts/{{alertToken}}

### Secure the account — revokes every session, forgets devices, returns reset_url (expects 200)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/security/login-alerts/{{alertToken}}/secure

### Secure again — the link is single-use (expects 410 {"error":"token_used"})
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/security/login-alerts/{{alertToken}}/secure

### Unknown or malformed token (expects 404 {"error":"not_found"})
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/security/login-alerts/not-a-token
